{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122018","id":4185825054,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc75fp8e","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122018","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122018.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122018.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122018","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122018/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122018/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122018/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/b8ad254425855f68f72d6cdc7e22fac4882c29cf","number":122018,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Fix out of bounds errors when reloading edited scene","user":{"login":"Prawnya","id":170275512,"node_id":"U_kgDOCiYyuA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/170275512?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Prawnya","html_url":"https://github.com/Prawnya","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Prawnya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Prawnya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Prawnya/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Prawnya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Prawnya/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Prawnya/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Prawnya/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Prawnya/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Prawnya/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch. We will take care of backporting relevant fixes to older versions.\r\n\r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n\r\nUse of AI must be disclosed and should include a description of how it was used.\r\n-->\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #121929\r\n\r\nFixes two things that can cause out of bounds errors in `EditorData` and the scene editors `TabBar`, whenever an edited scene is reloaded, such as when a file this scene depends on is moved in the file system (see linked issue).\r\n\r\nFixes:\r\n1. The tabs of the scene editors `TabBar` were not being updated when the scene that is being reloaded is the currently edited scene.\r\n2. If the current edited scene is empty whenever a scene is reloaded, the reloaded scene would overwrite the empty scene, without accounting for the decrease in the total number of edited scenes. This can also cause the editor to crash if the empty scene is not the last tab.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\nNote that my fix for point 2 is to never overwrite an empty scene when reloading a scene. This makes more sense to me than the current behavior. e.g. moving a file shouldn't have the side effect of closing a tab in the scene editor.\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nProvide additional information and explanation of your PR, including areas that you are uncertain of or require special attention from reviewers. For examples, please read our pull request guidelines: https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/pull_requests/pull_request_guidelines.html#explain-your-contributions\r\n-->\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"to